  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Operational Capacity-Building Support for the Korea Disaster Relief Team (KDRT) Reserve Workforce</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to the request of the Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA), the project aims to provide tailored trainings on humanitarian assistance to enhance the response capacity of the Korea Disaster Relief Team (KDRT) reserve members and affiliated personnel including officials in related functions and NGO partners. The project&#x2019;s main objective is to improve the target beneficiaries&#x2019; comprehension of, and practical skills for, operating emergency responses in an immediate onset of a disaster, including security and safety management, coordination, key intervention areas, and other fundamental topics of humanitarian assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
